stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> DRAFT : author records statement, vendor and intended artefact

    DRAFT --> CAPTURED : research attaches a capture that meets the dual-capture rule<br>posture label set to declared, observed in product or claim posture
    DRAFT --> REJECTED : no artefact can carry the statement<br>or the only source is a search summary or a rival's comparison page

    CAPTURED --> CLEARED : rules CLR-02 to CLR-09 and CLR-12 to CLR-16 pass<br>instance fits a counsel-cleared template for its class
    CAPTURED --> COUNSEL : class is counsel-per-instance<br>capability absent, commercial terms, legal-comparative
    CAPTURED --> REJECTED : wording cannot be scoped to the artefact read

    COUNSEL --> CLEARED : counsel records clearance on the entry
    COUNSEL --> REJECTED : counsel refuses the phrasing in every form

    CLEARED --> PUBLISHED : capture still inside its age window on the day of use<br>our artefact linked as a claim use row
    CLEARED --> WITHDRAWN : capture expires before first use

    PUBLISHED --> WITHDRAWN : watch alert triaged as material<br>or the capture reaches its expiry date
    WITHDRAWN --> CAPTURED : fresh capture taken inside the withdrawal window
    WITHDRAWN --> RETIRED : the finding is superseded or killed<br>entry and reason kept, never deleted

    REJECTED --> RETIRED : kept as a record of what may not be said
    RETIRED --> [*]

    note right of WITHDRAWN
        Withdrawal fans out. Every claim use row is flagged
        within the withdrawal window and every live artefact
        carrying the claim is pulled or re-cleared.
        A claim is never deleted, so a killed claim
        cannot quietly return.
    end note

    note left of PUBLISHED
        Only PUBLISHED claims may appear outside the company.
        Export of a claim whose capture is outside the age
        window is blocked, not warned.
    end note
